{"id":"eaa1f360-a033-4b15-bfbd-805aaf5c921d","object":"chat.completion","created":1784884765,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if 'tokens' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing required fields')\\n    tokens = case['tokens']\\n    if not isinstance(tokens, list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in tokens):\\n        raise ValueError('tokens must be a list of strings')\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError('calls must be a list')\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not all(k in call for k in ('call_id','start','end','score','replacement_tokens')):\\n            raise ValueError('Call missing required fields')\\n        if not isinstance(call['call_id'], str):\\n            raise ValueError('call_id must be string')\\n        if not isinstance(call['start'], int) or not isinstance(call['end'], int):\\n            raise ValueError('start/end must be int')\\n        if not isinstance(call['score'], (int,float)):\\n            raise ValueError('score must be numeric')\\n        if not isinstance(call['replacement_tokens'], list) or not all(isinstance(t,str) for t in call['replacement_tokens']):\\n            raise ValueError('replacement_tokens must be list of strings')\\n        if call['start'] < 0 or call['end'] > len(tokens) or call['start'] >= call['end']:\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid span indices')\\n\\n    # Rank candidates: descending score, ascending start, ascending call_id\\n    ranked = sorted(calls, key=lambda c: (-c['score'], c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n\\n    # Greedy selection – no overlap allowed\\n    selected = []  # list of dicts with start, end, call_id, replacement_tokens\\n    for c in ranked:\\n        overlap = False\\n        for s in selected:\\n            # intervals [start, end) – half-open\\n            if c['start'] < s['end'] and c['end'] > s['start']:\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append(c)\\n\\n    # Order accepted calls by start for reporting\\n    selected_sorted_by_start = sorted(selected, key=lambda c: c['start'])\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected_sorted_by_start]\\n\\n    # Apply replacements from right to left\\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)\\n    for c in sorted(selected, key=lambda c: c['start'], reverse=True):\\n        result_tokens = result_tokens[:c['start']] + c['replacement_tokens'] + result_tokens[c['end']:]\\n\\n    return {\\n        'selected_call_ids': selected_call_ids,\\n        'tokens': result_tokens\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate a Python solve function that implements the described algorithm. The case payload has \"tokens\" (list of strings) and \"calls\" (list of dicts with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). We need to:\n\n1. Select calls: rank by descending score, then ascending start position, then call_id (presumably lexicographic? It says \"start position, then call ID\", but ranking: descending score, then start position, then call ID. Since start is a tie-breaker after score, but order for reporting is by source start. The greedy selection: reject any span overlapping an already selected span. Overlap if intervals overlap? Start inclusive? end exclusive? From typical use, start and end likely refer to token indices. The example: call a start=1, end=3 (tokens at indices 1,2? possibly end exclusive), call b start=2,end=5 (overlaps). So we need to check if intervals [start, end) overlap. Standard: overlapping if new_start < selected_end and new_end > selected_start. But care: endpoints. We'll assume [start, end) since tokens at indices start..end-1. The description \"apply replacements from right to left\" suggests after selection, we need to interleave replacement tokens with the original